{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_332","type":"reasoning","text":"Clean: 23 files, all intentional, no stray artifacts. Now let me double check that the .gitignore / repository-artifacts.json are unchanged (they are, \"same\" for .gitignore; let me confirm repository-artifacts.json too — it wasn't in the changed list, so unchanged). Good.\n\nNow, the acceptanceCriteria mentions \"凭据扫描 0 命中\" and \"SHA256SUMS 可回读\". Let me re-verify G02-SHA256SUMS still matches (I regenerated after the acceptance json edit — yes, verified MATCH).\n\nBut wait — after regenerating G02-SHA256SUMS, did I edit anything else that's in the manifest? The last edit was the scope.source field in g02-acceptance.json, which I re-hashed. Verified MATCH. Good.\n\nNow let me also run the ask: \"run relevant existing checks that do not install dependencies\". I ran: check-spec-lifecycle, validate-policy-docs, check-error-governance, check-local-paths (failed due to no git), check-test-coverage-baseline, harness validate/context/list, and my probe. Also check-repository-artifacts and check-duplicate-assets fail in this workspace because there's no .git — that's an environment limitation (the isolated checkout has no git), not something I introduced. I should report that honestly.\n\nLet me also make sure the AGENTS.md line count budget check: 185 ≤ 400. Good — no change needed to AGENTS.md.\n\nLet me reconsider whether the task expects AGENTS.md edits. The acceptance criteria says \"AGENTS.md 保持轻量路由入口（<=400 行）并指向 harness/specs 作为规范归属，不复制平行清单。\" Since it already satisfies this (185 lines, routes to harness/specs), and there's already a mention of harness/specs as policy home in the \"Agent Harness routing\" section. But should I add a reference to the new rule? The criteria emphasize \"不复制平行清单\" (don't copy a parallel list). Adding a rule pointer might arguably be fine but could risk growing the entry. Since the entry already says \"Durable AI coding policy lives under harness/specs/**\", and targetScope doesn't list AGENTS.md, I'll leave AGENTS.md untouched. Actually targetScope explicitly lists the files expected; AGENTS.md is NOT in targetScope. So no AGENTS.md change. Good.\n\nNow, one acceptance criterion: \"文档引用可解析：node scripts/validate-policy-docs.mjs 与 check-error-governance.mjs 仍 PASS.\" Done both PASS.\n\nAlso: \"只有一条 doc-gardening 规则且命名可执行检查（check-spec-lifecycle.mjs）；不新建第二份规范 source of truth.\" Done and probe-verified.\n\nNow let me verify the harness validate for the sealed packets with a real diff base. The CLI needs a git repo. Since there's no .git, `--no-diff` is the structural path and it passed.\n\nI should also reconsider: the acceptance criterion mentions \"干净候选定向测试... harness validate/dry-run 通过\". The dry-run fails because there's no git (invalid diff base origin/main). That's an environment limitation. I reported `--no-diff` validate results. I'll note the dry-run limitation in the summary.\n\nLet me clean up temp files and finalize. Also remove the leftover temp scripts in $env:TEMP? Not necessary (outside workspace).\n\nLet me do a final verification pass: run all checks I claim, in one go, and capture outputs.\n\nAlso I should double-check the `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/g02-spec-doc-gardening.md` mentions of line counts match (185 lines AGENTS, 519 specs, 472 archived). Verified via probe earlier: agentsLines 185. lifecycle count 519. archived 472. Good.\n\nOne more: the rule spec references `pnpm harness:specs:lifecycle` — exists in package.json line 102. Good. And requiredTests lists `node node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run tests/unit/spec-doc-gardening.test.ts`. Fine as a declaration.\n\nLet me finalize with a consolidated verification run."}}
